            namely to the constant terms, which take the same value (here: 9) for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w \colon W
          %p
            In contrast to this, assume now that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            is such there is at least one non-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+function"} constant function
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \to \mathbb{N}
            = succeed "-dependent" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi W
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi NumberOfPlanetsInSolarSystem
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  w \colon W \vdash NumberOfPlanetsInSolarSystem(w) \colon \mathbb{N}(w)
                  \\,.
          %p
            That is the formalization of the above example we consider, and it should be evident enough. Now we may step back and see what the
            %a{:href => "#InFirstOrderLogicAndTypeTheory"} above formalization
            produce from this.
          %p
            So consider the
            = succeed "-dependent" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi W
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 9
                  %mo =
                  %mi NumberOfPlanetsInTheSolarSystem
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Type
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  w \colon W \vdash (9 = NumberOfPlanetsInTheSolarSystem)(w) \colon Type
                  \\,.
          %p
            By the assumption that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi NumberOfPlanetsInTheSolarSystem
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} NumberOfPlanetsInTheSolarSystem(w)
            is not constant in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            it follows that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            of that dependent identity type is the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+type"} empty type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo □
                    %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Box_W
            applied to it:
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mo □
                      %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 9
                    %mo =
                    %mi NumberOfPlanetsInTheSolarSystem
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Box_W (9 = NumberOfPlanetsInTheSolarSystem)]
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/false"} false
          %p
            However, if we assume that there is one
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
            for which indeed
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi NumberOfPlanetsInTheSolarSystem
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} NumberOfPlanetsInTheSolarSystem(w)
            takes the value 9, then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum"} dependent sum
            over the dependent identity type contains that coincidence as a term, and so
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ♢
                    %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \diamondsuit_W
            of our dependent identity type is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+type"} inhabited
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mo ♢
                      %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 9
                    %mo =
                    %mi NumberOfPlanetsInTheSolarSystem
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\diamondsuit_W (9 = NumberOfPlanetsInTheSolarSystem)]
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/true"} true
          %p In English words, these formal consequences are to be pronounced as:
          %ol
            %li
              %p “It is false that it is necessary that the number of planets in the solar system is 9.”
            %li
              %p “It is true that it is possible that the number of planets in the solar system is 9.”
          %p Which is just as it should be.
          %p
            Similarly, the
            = succeed "-dependent" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi W
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi NumberOfPlanetsInTheSolarSystem
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 7
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  w \colon W \vdash (NumberOfPlanetsInTheSolarSystem \gt 7)(w) \colon \mathbb{N}(w)
          %p
            is only going to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+type"} inhabited
            if indeed the value
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi NumberOfPlanetsInTheSolarSystem
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} NumberOfPlanetsInTheSolarSystem(w)
            is greater than 7 for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w\colon W
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mo □
                      %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi NumberOfPlanetsInTheSolarSystem
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 7
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Box_W (NumberOfPlanetsInTheSolarSystem \gt 7)]
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/false"} false
          %p hence
          %ul
            %li “It is false that it is necessary that the number of planets in the solar system is greater than 7.”
          %p
            %br/
          %h4#ModalQuantumLogic Quantum modal logic
          %blockquote
            %p under construction
          %p
            We discuss
            %sup#fnref:1
              %a{:href => "#fn:1", :rel => "footnote"} 1
            the modal logic induced from base change of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+types"} dependent types
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Globally"} above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+linear+types"} dependent linear types
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+sets"} finite sets
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/family+of+finite+types"}> family of finite types
            ) — to find a natural
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+logic"} modal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+logic"} quantum logic
            (and in fact a natural
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+programming+language"} quantum programming language
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+circuits"} quantum circuits
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+circuits+via+dependent+linear+types"} quantum circuits via dependent linear types
            for more on this).
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            Given a base
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            (which we take to be
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/family+of+finite+types"} finite
          #eq:FiniteBaseType.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (5)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi FinType
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  B \;\in\; FinType
                  \\,,
          %p
            write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi LinType
                    %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LinType_B
            for the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+linear+types"} dependent linear types
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mo •
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LinType
                    %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ↔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi b
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mi b
                  %mo :
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} LinType
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathscr{H}_\bullet \,\in\, \mathrm{LinType}_B
                  \\;\;\;\;\;\;\leftrightarrow\;\;\;\;\;\;
                  b : B \;\;\vdash\;\; \mathscr{H}_b : \mathrm{LinType}
                  \\,.
          %p
            The intended
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            is obtained by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+between+type+theory+and+category+theory"} interpreting
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H}_\bullet
            as a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+set"} indexed set
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+spaces"} complex vector spaces
            (or rather:
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+inner+product+spaces"} Hermitian inner product spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+dimensional+vector+space"} finite dimensional
            (
            %a{:href => "Hilbert+space#FiniteDimensionalInnerProductSpaces"}> hence
            \: as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+spaces"} Hilbert spaces
            if positive definite), though this finite-dimensionality condition of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H}_b
            is not used in the following (as opposed to the finiteness condition on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            We assume that our
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+linear+type+theory"} dependent linear type theory
            realizes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            of linear types along maps of non-linear base types in the form of
            = succeed "-type" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wirthm%C3%BCller+context"} Wirthmüller
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/yoga+of+six+operations"} yoga of six operations
          %div{:style => "margin: -30px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/QCwthLHT-BaseChange-221001.jpg", :width => "680px"}/
          %p
            Moreover, we assume that along maps with
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal
            map
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to \ast
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            agrees with the right
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ambidextrous+adjunction"}> ambidexterity
            ”, so that both give the dependent
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/biproduct"} biproduct
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes_{b : B}
            over
            = succeed "):" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} stability
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo !
                  %msub
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mo •
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mo •
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mo :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mi b
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mtext (biproducts)
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathrm{stability}
                  \\;:\;
                  (p_B)_! \mathscr{H}_\bullet
                  \\;\;\simeq\;\;
                  (p_B)_\ast \mathscr{H}_\bullet
                  \\;\;=:\;\;
                  \\underset{b : B}{\bigoplus}
                  \\mathscr{H}_b
                  \\;\;\;
                  \\text{(biproducts)}
          %p
            Curiously, in terms of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+logic"} modal logic
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gell-Mann+principle"} Gell-Mann principle
            of quantum physics, in that it means:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mtext The
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mtext possible
                        %mtd
                          %mtext is
                        %mtd
                          %mtext necessary
                        %mtd
                          %mtext and hence
                        %mtd
                          %mtext actualized
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo ♢
                          %msub
                            %mi ℋ
                            %mo •
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                          %mo □
                          %msub
                            %mi ℋ
                            %mo •
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mphantom
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo −
                              %mi ϵ
                              %mphantom
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo −
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi ℋ
                            %mrow
                              %mo •
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mtext with some probability
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\llap{\text{The}}\;\text{possible}
                  \&amp;
                  \\text{is}
                  \&amp;
                  \\text{necessary}
                  \&amp;
                  \\text{and hence}
                  \&amp;
                  \\text{actualized}
                  \\\
                  \\diamondsuit \mathcal{H}_\bullet
                  \&amp;
                  \\simeq
                  \&amp;
                  \\Box \mathcal{H}_\bullet
                  \&amp;
                  \\xrightarrow{\phantom{--} \epsilon \phantom{--}}
                  \&amp;
                  \\mathcal{H}_{
                  \\bullet
                  \\;
                  \\mathrlap{\text{with some probability}}
                  }
                  }
          %p
            Both these assumptions are verified in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+homotopy+type+theory"} linear homotopy type theory
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "dependent+linear+type+theory#Riley22Thesis"} Riley (2022), §2.4
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            in (a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type-theoretic+model+category"} type-theoretic model category
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presenting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"}
