          %div{:style => "margin: -20px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/QCwthLHT-QuantumModalUnits-230806.jpg", :width => "810px"}/
          %p
            In the context of linear types not just
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi B
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p_B)^\ast
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+functor"} monadic
            = succeed "/" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p_B)_!
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p_B)_\ast
            (for details see the
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a{:href => "function+monad#QuantumReaderMonad"} quantum reader monad
            %a{:href => "#PotentialityAsMonadicDescent"} above
            enhances to the following situation:
          #eq:DependentLinearTypesAsIndefiniteLinearTypes.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (8)
            %code.maruku-mathml
          %div{:style => "margin: -10px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/LinearTypesAsModalModules-221113.jpg", :width => "810px"}/
          %p
            %br/
          #eq:NotationalConvention.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (9)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mtext It is convenient and meaningful to declare notational conventions to:
                  %mphantom
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo −
