                          %mi LinType
                          %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p_B)^\ast \colon LinType \to LinType_B
          %p
            Thereby, the definiteness/randomness modalities in relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/necessity+and+possibility"} necessity and possibility
            of classical modal logic (
            %a{:href => "#ClassicalModalLogic"}> above
            ) may be expressed in quantum modal logic by:
          %div{:style => "margin: -10px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/DefinitelyRandomlyViaPossiblyNecessarily.jpg", :width => "210px"}/
          %p Considering the basic dependent linear type
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo •
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
